# Hearth Elemental: "This spell costs {X} less to cast, where X is the number of cards in your graveyard that are instant cards,
# sorcery cards, and/or have an Adventure." Bot1 casts Stoke Genius (Hearth Elemental's Adventure, {1}{R}): "Discard your hand, then
# draw two cards" puts Bonecrusher Giant (a creature card that has an Adventure), Shock (an instant), Ornithopter (an artifact
# creature) and an Island in the graveyard, so X is 2 - the creature with an Adventure counts, the Ornithopter and the Island do not.
# Hearth Elemental, now in exile, is cast from there for {6} less 2 = {3}{R}: Bot1 taps exactly four Moxen and nothing is left in
# its mana pool (a third counted card would leave mana over, a lower X would leave the spell unpaid). Stoke Genius itself cost
# {1}{R}, the graveyard being empty then.

